WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:09.840
"You did it, Wilbur," cried Orville as his brother landed their invention.

2
00:00:09.841 --> 00:00:17.803
"Finally, we are successful. October the fifth of 1905 will go down in history," replied his brother.

3
00:00:17.804 --> 00:00:23.986
"Today you flew the world's first working airplane. You flew more than 24 miles.

4
00:00:23.987 --> 00:00:32.131
This invention is really going to change the world," exclaimed Orville. "And we invented it!"

5
00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:37.364
The Wright brothers were true inventors who spent their lives trying to build better machines.

6
00:00:37.365 --> 00:00:40.637
Wilbur and Orville were extremely intelligent men.

7
00:00:40.638 --> 00:00:46.942
Unlike most scientists, however, they did not go to a university. They were self-taught geniuses.

8
00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:51.710
Wilbur was a fantastic student and was registered to attend Yale University.

9
00:00:51.711 --> 00:00:55.754
But in 1886 he got hit in the face with a hockey stick.

10
00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:59.693
The injury was so bad that it took him almost a year to recover.

11
00:00:59.694 --> 00:01:04.374
By the time he recovered, his mother had become very sick.

12
00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:09.713
So instead of going back to school, Wilbur spent the next year looking after his mother.

13
00:01:09.714 --> 00:01:12.790
Whenever he had a spare moment, he would read.

14
00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:16.401
During this time Orville also lost interest in school.

15
00:01:16.402 --> 00:01:20.719
He found a part-time job in a small printing shop.

16
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:27.405
Orville knew that he could make a lot of money if he had a professional printing press, but it was far too expensive.

17
00:01:27.406 --> 00:01:31.213
So together the two brothers built their own printing press.

18
00:01:31.214 --> 00:01:38.787
They made it almost entirely from old junk that they found themselves, including a broken tombstone.

19
00:01:38.788 --> 00:01:45.033
Soon their printing business was a success, so the brothers decided to build an even larger printing press.

20
00:01:45.034 --> 00:01:50.741
Their second press was able to print one thousand sheets an hour, which was very fast at the time.

21
00:01:50.742 --> 00:01:58.517
However, the Wright brothers were inventors and not printing men, and they soon became bored with the printing business.

22
00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:04.206
In 1892 the Wright brothers became interested in a new sport: bicycle riding.

23
00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:11.108
Because they were excellent mechanics, they soon had their own bicycle shop and became very good at fixing bicycles.

24
00:02:11.109 --> 00:02:18.855
After a few years, Orville and Wilbur decided that they could build better bicycles than the ones they sold.

25
00:02:18.856 --> 00:02:22.537
So they designed two bicycles that became very popular.

26
00:02:22.538 --> 00:02:29.119
The Wright brothers were making a lot of money in the bicycle business, but making money was not what they liked best.

27
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.997
What they loved was to learn and invent.

28
00:02:32.998 --> 00:02:39.786
During the next ten years, the Wright brothers would invent what almost everyone thought was impossible: the airplane.

29
00:02:39.787 --> 00:02:47.621
In 1896 Wilbur read a newspaper article about a famous German pilot who died flying a plane he had designed.

30
00:02:47.622 --> 00:02:52.768
From that moment, he became very interested in the art of flying.

31
00:02:52.769 --> 00:03:00.225
After careful thought, Wilbur and Orville guessed that the problem with the German pilot's airplane was that it had no controls.

32
00:03:00.226 --> 00:03:04.040
Of course, the Wright brothers thought they could design one that worked.

33
00:03:04.041 --> 00:03:09.191
The first thing the Wright brothers did was to read everything that they could find on aviation.

34
00:03:09.192 --> 00:03:16.926
One day while reading, Wilbur saw birds flying, and he noticed that they were constantly moving their wings to keep themselves balanced.

35
00:03:16.927 --> 00:03:21.297
This was the big clue that he needed.

36
00:03:21.298 --> 00:03:25.971
The Wright brothers decided to build a glider, that is, a plane with no engine.

37
00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:29.462
It had wings that moved so that they could control and turn it.

38
00:03:29.463 --> 00:03:33.543
The first two gliders that the Wright brothers built were not very successful.

39
00:03:33.544 --> 00:03:39.613
In fact, the second one was so bad that Wilbur was almost killed trying to fly it.

40
00:03:39.614 --> 00:03:46.238
After the crash, Wilbur said to his brother, "Not in a thousand years will man ever fly."

41
00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:51.574
However, after being encouraged by other engineers, they decided to try again.

42
00:03:51.575 --> 00:03:57.418
In 1902, after careful research, the Wright brothers' third glider was a success.

43
00:03:57.419 --> 00:04:01.706
Finally they had built a plane that they could control.

44
00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:06.846
The next step was to build an airplane with an engine, so that it could fly on its own power.

45
00:04:06.847 --> 00:04:13.897
The brothers asked many engine companies to help them build an engine and propeller for their plane, but no one would help them.

46
00:04:13.898 --> 00:04:19.375
So they decided to make their own engine and invented a method for making propellers.

47
00:04:19.376 --> 00:04:24.928
On December 17, 1903, the Wright brothers' first airplane was completed.

48
00:04:24.929 --> 00:04:30.371
The Flyer made four very short flights, but then crashed and was completely destroyed.

49
00:04:30.372 --> 00:04:36.773
The Wright brothers rebuilt the Flyer and called it the Flyer 2. It worked but had many problems.

50
00:04:36.774 --> 00:04:41.492
So in 1905, the Wrights completely rebuilt their aircraft.

51
00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:49.468
The Flyer 3 was amazing. It was the first flying machine capable of taking off and flying through the air on its own power.

52
00:04:49.469 --> 00:04:53.887
It could rise, descend, and turn in any direction that the pilot wanted.

53
00:04:53.888 --> 00:04:59.234
Wilbur flew the plane over 24 miles and landed only when his plane ran out of gas.

54
00:04:59.235 --> 00:05:05.914
It was an invention destined to change the world.
